-- The farm's main() returns `api`; we can't reach the internal `import` from outside.
-- So we re-import the same modules from ReplicatedStorage? No — the farm's modules are
-- compiled into its closure. Instead we expose them via the loader it already exposes.
-- The farm's `api.Catalog` / `api.Icons` / `api.Config` / `api.State` are public; the
-- task modules are not. So COCOON must be launched as a second file that the farm
-- loads in the same environment. To keep it simple here, we wrap the task calls we
-- need through `Farm.Config` (settings) and mimic the task behavior only when the
-- farm API is absent. For the full integration, put this file's body inside the
-- farm's main() after `api` is created, or have the loader pass `import` in.
--
-- Below: the local task functions COCOON needs that don't depend on the farm internals,
-- plus a thin wrapper that calls the farm's own task runners via the modules it loads
-- through `import` when the loader makes it available.

-- Try to grab the farm's internal import via its loader (if the farm was launched with
-- `getgenv().AdoptMeFarmSettings`, it also stashed `_G.__FarmImport` = import).
local FarmImport = env.__FarmImport
local Tasks, EventTasks, HouseTasks, WhereBear
if type(FarmImport) == "function" then
    local ok1, m1 = pcall(FarmImport, "Game/Tasks")
    if ok1 then Tasks = m1 end
    local ok2, m2 = pcall(FarmImport, "Game/EventTasks")
    if ok2 then EventTasks = m2 end
    local ok3, m3 = pcall(FarmImport, "Game/HouseTasks")
    if ok3 then HouseTasks = m3 end
    local ok4, m4 = pcall(FarmImport, "Game/WhereBear")
    if ok4 then WhereBear = m4 end
end

